on/aggregate/Median.java-2365:2469-2523:2540,2549:2569,2586:2775","promptId":"#73AKB","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2365,"endPos":2469,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":119,"length":105}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2523,"endPos":2540,"startLine":68,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":68,"endLineOffset":25,"length":18},{"pos":2549,"endPos":2569,"startLine":69,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":69,"endLineOffset":28,"length":21},{"pos":2586,"endPos":2775,"startLine":71,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":73,"endLineOffset":118,"length":190}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java--147120:150829","promptId":"#E2FM7","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":147120,"endPos":150829,"startLine":3617,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":3685,"endLineOffset":5,"length":3710}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java--5928:6219","promptId":"#NFBQ1","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5928,"endPos":6219,"startLine":124,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":132,"endLineOffset":5,"length":292}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":103,"line":103,"comment_lines":["[][103]"],"review_comment":["use field.fold() since the field can be an expression such as 1 + 1 and you want to return the surrogate before the rest of the optimizer rules kick in.","Would love to just fold, but folding here is not safe unless we check if this will fold to `null`, first. That would require duplicating logic from `FoldNull`, though, which I\u0027d prefer to avoid.\r\n\r\n(Our evaluators cannot deal with null literals in general, and folding here results in the following exception when running e.g. `count(to_double(null))`:\r\n```\r\nillegal data type [null]\r\norg.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException: illegal data type [null]\r\n\tat __randomizedtesting.SeedInfo.seed([DBCF40F13A40EC92:539B7F2B94BC816A]:0)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.CsvTests.stats.Asdf(stats.csv-spec:1708)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:43)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:39)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.evaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:65)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.toEvaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:105)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.evaluator.mapper.EvaluatorMapper.fold(EvaluatorMapper.java:48)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.EsqlScalarFunction.fold(EsqlScalarFunction.java:30)\r\n```\r\n)","Consider the rare case of count(1+1) - there might be count(1+null). This can be moved to a separate issue though to not block this one.","It makes sense to add more tests to account for these cases where an expression is evaluated, esp. to `null`. I\u0027ll do that in another PR, as this one should be backported to 8.14 as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nThese cases are covered in this PR, it\u0027s just that they result in an extra eval+projection.\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS count(1+null)\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecomes something equivalent to\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS x \u003d count(*)\r\n| EVAL `count(1+null)` \u003d COALESCE(MV_COUNT(1+null), 0) * x\r\n| KEEP `count(1+null)`\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich after folding becomes a multiplication of `count(*)` with 0. If we wanted to, we could further optimize this case to avoid the `count(*)` as well.","Opened a PR with additional tests: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/107888"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","id":37860,"created_at":"2024-04-22T07:12:26Z","original_position":42,"side":"RIGHT","position":42,"submitted_on_commit":"496a2448383e0316baf22f3f3605daee2061682f","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,4 +93,30 @@ public Nullability nullable() {\n     protected TypeResolution resolveType() {\n         return EsqlTypeResolutions.isExact(field(), sourceText(), DEFAULT);\n     }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public Expression surrogate() {\n+        var s \u003d source();\n+        var field \u003d field();\n+\n+        if (field.foldable()) {\n+            if (field instanceof Literal l) {","submitted_line":103},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for handling foldable expressions in the `surrogate` method seems correct but could be improved for clarity and maintainability. Specifically:\n- The comment about normalizing COUNT(*), COUNT(), COUNT(\"foobar\"), COUNT(1) as COUNT(*) is a TODO that should either be addressed or removed if it\u0027s no longer relevant.\n- The logic for handling foldable fields in `Count` and `CountDistinct` could be refactored to avoid code duplication. Consider extracting the common logic into a helper method.\n- In `Count`, the commented-out return statement suggests a potential optimization that